A||||0||Fformula88||Went to the Pierce-Arrow meet!  Awesome!||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||07-15-2001||08:22 PM||||This weekend here in Buffalo was the Pierce-Arrow meet commemorating the opening of a Pierce-Arrow museum here!  They must have had a couple hundred Pierce-Arrows, and thousands of people turned out to look at them.  Woodrow Wilson's presidential car and Babe Ruth's P-A were both in attendance.  It was amazing to see how many had been restored, and showed up for the event considering the relatively low production numbers and age of the vehicles.<P>For anyone who may not know what they are... Pierce-Arrow was a car company from Early 1900 until 1938 or so.  They built what many people considered some of the finest luxury cars made.  The company and the manufacturing were also based here in Buffalo, which is why they opened the museum up here.<P>Hopefully there will still be some nice Fiero's around when they are 80 years old too!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
